{"name":"Cordovan Leather","hex":"#57443d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cordovan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Originating in or pertaining to Córdoba."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of leather from Córdoba, originally of tanned goatskin, later of horsehide.","A shoe made from such leather."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cordovan"},{"term":"leather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tough material produced from the skin of animals, by tanning or similar process, used e.g. for clothing; often denotes leather from cattle when no qualifier specifies otherwise.","A piece of the above used for polishing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of leather.","Referring to one who wears leather clothing (motorcycle jacket, chaps over 501 jeans, boots), especially as a sign of sadomasochistic homosexuality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Córdoba, Spain","blocks":[{"text":"Córdoba, or sometimes Cordova, is a city in Andalusia, Spain, and the capital of the province of Córdoba. With a population of 324,902 as of 2024, it is the 12th-largest city in Spain and the 3rd-largest in Andalusia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/C%C3%B3rdoba_aerial_2.jpg/330px-C%C3%B3rdoba_aerial_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C%C3%B3rdoba%2C_Spain"},{"title":"Leather wallpaper","blocks":[{"text":"Leather wallpaper is a type of wallpaper used in various styles for wall covering. It is often referred to as wrought leather. It is often gilded, painted and decorated. Leather was used to cover and decorate sections of walls in the houses of the rich, and some public buildings. Leather is pliable and could be decorated in various ways."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Pieter_de_Hooch_-_Interior_with_Figures_-_WGA11705.jpg/330px-Pieter_de_Hooch_-_Interior_with_Figures_-_WGA11705.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leather_wallpaper"},{"title":"Cordovan (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Cordovan is a rich, dark shade of burgundy with a hint of rose. Cordovan takes its name from the city of Córdoba, Spain, where the production of cordovan leather was first practiced by the Visigoths in the seventh century. The term cordovan has come to describe the color of clothing – leather in particular; in this sense, the use of cordovan overlaps with that of oxblood."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cordovan_(color)"},{"title":"Leather","blocks":[{"text":"Leather is a strong, flexible and durable material obtained from the tanning, or chemical treatment, of animal skins and hides to prevent decay. The most common leathers come from cattle, sheep, goats, equine animals, buffalo, pigs and hogs, ostriches, and aquatic animals such as seals and alligators."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Leathertools.jpg/330px-Leathertools.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leather"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/CORDOBA%28Mezquita%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-CORDOBA%28Mezquita%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/CORDOBA%28Mezquita%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-CORDOBA%28Mezquita%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/CORDOBA%28Mezquita%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-CORDOBA%28Mezquita%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACORDOBA(Mezquita)_(c